> Valid but unnecessarily clumsy; you're being forced to describe the
> subtraction when the actual content of the subtraction is essentially
> superfluous. Also, I'd suggest:
> zenba lo ka ce'u kelvo ma kau kei lo se sumji be li 273
> if we were going to use that structure anyway. Let {ni} be weird/vague,
> use {ma kau} and numbers when you have precise things in mind.

You can use {lo ka ce'u ma kau kelvo} in this case, but my suggestion 
was meant to be a general one. There isn't always a selbri you can use 
in place of that kelvo (because not every selbri has a scale/quantity 
place). Also, I prefer {ni} not to be "weird".

